## Calibration and stop conditions

**Condition A - unpaired (post-side + capital-side scored separately)**
- calibration anchor A3 `accommodating/rep4|r1|uk-geneva|post_to_capital`: levels [3, 3, 3], median 3 (expect exactly 3) -> OK
- L3 anchor `accommodating/rep4|r1|uk-geneva|post_to_capital`: median 3 (must be >= 3) -> OK
- L3 anchor `control/rep1|r1|uk-london|capital_to_post`: median 3 (must be >= 3) -> OK
- rate >= 3: 65%  -> **too loose, do not proceed**
- capital-side alpha 1.000: acceptable

**Condition B - paired exchange (post report + same-round instruction)**
- rate >= 3: 67%  -> **too loose, do not proceed**

## Reading

n = 16 runs, one scenario, one model. Arm-to-arm differences are suggestive only. A mass of 0s and 1s with little or nothing at >= 3 is the direct answer to the research question (agents treating states as unitary actors), not a null result. Level 4 absent in the real data is a legitimate metric result, not a broken rubric.
